       "text": "I'm not going to enter this one. You've confirmed the dose, but you haven't given a clinical reason for it. A single 50 mg dose is far above the 10 mg maximum, and I can't find an indication that would justify it. The risk of serious harm is high, and a transcription error like 5 mg becoming 50 mg is a common way these mistakes happen.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** Give me 5 mg or 10 mg once daily and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Get a second review.** If you think a nonstandard dose is needed, discuss it with a pharmacist or your attending first. If they approve it, tell me who and why, and I'll put that in the order note.\n- **Consider other options.** If the goal is more blood pressure control, adding a second agent from a different class is usually safer than going above the amlodipine maximum.\n\nI can enter the order as soon as you choose one."
